      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/cricket-india-dominate-first-test-by-taking-lead-of-178-runs-against-sri-lanka/",
      "date": "Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:00:17 IST",
      "content": "In Men’s Cricket, Hosts Sri Lanka were 84 for 4 in their second innings against India at stumps on the fourth day of the first Test in Galle. Sonal Dinusha and Dhananjaya de Silva remained at the crease when stumps were drawn this evening. For India, Manav Suthar took two wickets. Earlier in the day, India were bowled out for 193 in their second innings, setting Sri Lanka a target of 372 runs. Rishabh Pant top scored with 66 runs off 69 deliveries, including two sixes and eight fours. He also became the first Indian player and only the fourth in the world to hit 100 sixes in Test cricket. Pant reached the milestone in just his 51st Test, becoming the fastest player to complete 100 sixes in the format. For Sri Lanka, Asitha Fernando claimed four wickets, while Prabath Jayasuriya picked up two. On the previous day, Indian bowlers bowled Sri Lanka out for 284 in their first innings. Manav Suthar was the pick of the Indian attack, claiming four wickets, while Ravindra Jadeja took three. For Sri Lanka, Sonal Dinusha scored his maiden Test century, while Niroshan Dickwella contributed 80 runs. India were dismissed for 462 in their first innings. Devdutt Padikkal top-scored with 167, while KL Rahul made 82 and Dhruv Jurel scored 51. For Sri Lanka, Prabath Jayasuriya took four wickets, Keshara Nuwantha claimed three, and Asitha Fernando picked up two. The second and final Test of the series will be played in Colombo from the 23rd of this month.",
      "content_chars": 1460,
      "content_words": 254,
      "type": "Article"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "BWF Badminton World Championships: India’s Unnati Hooda advances to women’s singles second round 7 hours ago 98",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/bwf-badminton-world-championships-indias-unnati-hooda-advances-to-womens-singles-second-round/",
      "date": "Tue, 18 Aug 2026 15:00:18 IST",
      "content": "In the BWF Badminton World Championships, India’s Unnati Hooda has advanced to the women’s singles second round after defeating Myanmar’s Thet Htar Thuzar in straight games at the Indira Gandhi Indoor Stadium in New Delhi. In a closely contested first game, the Indian shuttler edged past her opponent by 22-20, while she stepped up the second game, winning it comfortably by 21-16. She will face the 13th-seeded Michelle Li of Canada in the Round of 32. Meanwhile, the match between the Indian pair of Ashith Surya and Amrutha Pramuthesh and Turkey’s Emre Sonmez and Yasemen Bektas in the mixed doubles event is underway. The Indian duo has won the first game, 21-16. Later in the evening, ace shuttler Lakshya Sen will face Collins Filimon of Austria in the men’s singles first round. The Indian pair of Treesa Jolly and Gayatri Gopichand will face the United States’ Lauren Lam and Allison Lee in the second round of women’s doubles. While Kavipriya Selvam and Simran Singhi will take on Bulgaria’s Stefani Stoeva and Gabriela Stoeva in another women’s doubles second round. Earlier today, India’s Rohan Kapoor and Ruthvika Shivani Gadde faced a defeat against the Canadian pair of Jonathan Lai and Crystal Lai in the mixed doubles first round. After winning the first game by 22-20, the Indian duo lost the next two games by 19-21 and 17-21.",
      "content_chars": 1345,
      "content_words": 226,
      "type": "Article"
    },
    {
      "source": "News On AIR",
      "title": "UP: Free medical treatment up to 5 lakh and increase in DA for Provincial Armed Guards announced 2 hours ago 55",
      "url": "https://newsonair.gov.in/up-free-medical-treatment-up-to-5-lakh-and-increase-in-da-for-provincial-armed-guards-announced/",
      "date": "Tue, 18 Aug 2026 20:00:28 IST",
      "content": "The Uttar Pradesh government has announced that Provincial Armed Guard (PRD) personnel and their families will get free treatment up to Rs 5 lakh annually and also have their daily duty allowance increased. Chief Minister Yogi Adityanath, who had increased the duty allowance three times during his tenure, announced the fourth increase at the PRD personnel conference in Gorakhpur and said PRD personnel will now receive a daily duty allowance of rupees 600 instead of rupees 500. At the PRD personnel conference organized at Yogiraj Baba Gambhirnath Auditorium today, CM Yogi distributed cashless medical facility cards to PRD volunteers and launched the ‘Mukhyamantri PRD Cashless Chikitsa Yojana’. He also laid the foundation stone, by pressing a button on the remote, for the multi-story PRD barracks to be constructed in Lucknow at a cost of around rupees 23 crore. Addressing the gathering, the Chief Minister made a new announcement for PRD personnel. The Chief Minister said that PRD volunteers, established in 1948, received a daily duty allowance of rupees 250 until 2019. In 2019, he increased it to rupees 375, and in 2022, it was increased to rupees 395. The allowance was increased again in 2025 and raised to rupees 500 per day.",
      "content_chars": 1244,
      "content_words": 202,
      "type": "Article"
    },
